  "reasoning": "Statewide, Utah has a Cook Partisan Voting Index of R+11, indicating it votes about 11 points more Republican than the national average in recent presidential elections[1][10]. In addition, historical descriptions classify Utah as a deep red state that has voted Republican in every presidential election since 1968 and list CPVI figures as high as R+13\u2013R+20, underscoring a long-standing, lopsided GOP advantage[10]. I did not find within-the-last-45-days polling for specific 2026 federal matchups, so the best quantitative baseline is that Utah\u2019s recent federal Republican margins are on the order of 20 points or more, which I use as a conservative estimate of the structural advantage rather than a specific current race result[10].",
